[gd_resource type="Sky" load_steps=3 format=3 uid="uid://d7gubrangesky"]

; The sky over Glowworm Grounds, and the reason the map is worth standing on.
;
; It was the island's night: `enchanted_sky.gdshader` with a moon pinned to the
; map's own Sun, a flat sheet of cloud, stars, an aurora and a glow band over
; the trees to the south. That was correct — the range is a cleared bog a mile
; from Whisperbloom Hollow and it would be strange under a different moon — and
; it gave a range you could barely see the ground of, which is the one thing a
; range must not be. So this is **the same bog an hour earlier**: nine degrees
; of sun north-north-east, a cotton-candy sky, and the glowworm lanterns just
; coming on.
;
; The shader is `range_sky.gdshader`. Its header carries the argument for why
; the clouds are a **stylised 2D field on the dome** rather than the marched
; heightfield Kopje uses; the short of it is that a slab seen edge-on from eye
; height can only ever give shelves, and it was measured three ways before it
; was believed. All the tuning lives here. What the numbers are for:
;
;   the three stops       apricot at the skyline (`horizon_color`), rose through
;                         the middle of the dome (`mid_color`, centred at
;                         `mid_height` 0.38 of the way up the ramp and 0.5
;                         wide), soft periwinkle overhead (`zenith_color`). The
;                         zenith was a saturated 0.22/0.45/0.84 blue first and
;                         read as a hole punched in the sunset.
;   the glory             `sun_aureole_falloff` **100 against Kopje's 190**, at
;                         0.85 energy. A nine-degree sun is seen through about
;                         six times the air a noon one is, so a wide aureole is
;                         the honest picture as well as the pretty one. It was
;                         70 at 1.5 to begin with and the horizon went white.
;   the disc              `sun_energy` 9.0 against Kopje's 22, because a low sun
;                         is reddened by what it comes through — and because the
;                         lanes point near it. `sun_angular_size` 0.021 is twice
;                         the real sun: a low sun reads bigger, and at 0.0093 it
;                         is four pixels.
;   which sun             `sun_follow_light` is **on**, so the disc and the
;                         glory are pinned to the map's own `Sun` and cannot
;                         disagree with the shadows. `sun_direction` is the
;                         fallback for a scene opened without its light, and it
;                         is kept equal to that node's +Z:
;                         `range_map._check_sun_and_sky` prints how far apart
;                         they are and the gate reads it. That check exists
;                         because the two were sixty degrees apart for a whole
;                         pass and no render said so.
;   the puff field        `puff_scale` 1.5 dome units per noise tile on a
;                         `puff_dome_k` 0.75 projection, `puff_coverage` 0.68.
;                         Coverage is the map of the sky and it was found by
;                         bracketing: 0.36 gives a mackerel sky of small clots
;                         over the whole dome, 0.50 a connected chain, 0.60 a
;                         chain with holes, 0.68 four to six separate clouds
;                         with rose sky between them and under them. `puff_warp`
;                         0.45 is what stops them being round blobs and
;                         `puff_billow` 0.60 is the cauliflower knob — the two
;                         folded octaves that give a lobed edge instead of a
;                         smooth one.
;   the light on them     `puff_light` 9.0 over a `puff_light_step` of 0.09
;                         dome units. It is a gain on a finite difference, so it
;                         wants to land where the answer is a **terminator**
;                         rather than a line: at 20 the two taps read as a
;                         stencil with a hard edge across every cloud, at 9 the
;                         lit side fades into the shadow the way a cumulus does.
;                         `puff_belly` 0.75 over a longer step, because an
;                         underside is a broader feature than a shoulder.
;   the rim               `puff_rim` 2.6 in a warm peach. At nine degrees the
;                         sunward edge of a cloud is most of what you see of it.
;   the second layer      the same field at `puff2_scale` 1.6 and its own patch,
;                         at 0.6 opacity: the small fair-weather cumulus between
;                         and under the big ones. One layer at any coverage is
;                         one size of cloud everywhere.
;   which weather         `puff_offset` and `puff2_offset`. The field is a fixed
;                         function of direction and time and the camera sits at
;                         its origin, so without an offset the sky over this map
;                         is whatever the hash does near (0, 0), and the only
;                         other way to change it is `puff_scale`, which changes
;                         the clouds as well as which ones you get.
;   drift                 0.004 dome units per second, about eight minutes to
;                         cross the visible sky: slow enough to be weather, fast
;                         enough that a player waiting out a respawn sees it.
;   the lower hemisphere  `ground_*` is **not scenery**. `range_env.tres` takes
;                         100% of its ambient from this dome, so the bottom half
;                         of it is the only light reaching anything that faces
;                         down — the lodge roof over the eight spawn pads most
;                         of all. It was lifted twice for exactly that.
;
; INCREMENTAL, like every sky here: nothing in it moves fast enough for one
; radiance mip a frame to be visible.

[ext_resource type="Shader" path="res://resources/shaders/range_sky.gdshader" id="1_range_sky_shader"]

